(TREASURY AND CORPORATE FINANCE STRATEGIC MEMORANDUM) '
() '
(Ref: TC-FIN-2026-402 | Distribution: Executive Committee & Audit) '
(Board) '
() '
(1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY: LIQUIDITY PROFILE AND WORKING CAPITAL) '
() '
(This memorandum establishes the updated treasury capital forecast) '
(for the upcoming fiscal quarters. Consolidated operating cash flow) '
(rose 11.2% year-over-year to $86.4 million, driven primarily by) '
(optimized accounts receivable collections and rigorous inventory) '
(turnover controls across regional fulfillment centers.) '
() '
(Cash and cash equivalents, including marketable short-term) '
(securities, total $142.8 million. Unutilized capacity under our) '
(syndicated revolving credit facility stands at $75.0 million with a) '
(consortium of five tier-one financial institutions, expiring) '
(December 2028.) '
() '
(2. CASH CONVERSION CYCLE \(CCC\) METRICS AND OPTIMIZATION) '
() '
(Days Sales Outstanding \(DSO\) improved from 48.2 days to 39.5 days) '
(following automated invoice dispute workflows. Days Inventory) '
(Outstanding \(DIO\) reduced from 62.1 days to 54.0 days through) '
(predictive just-in-time replenishment. Days Payable Outstanding) '
(\(DPO\) was renegotiated to 60.0 days with core tier-1 vendors,) '
(generating a net CCC compression of 16.8 days.) '
() '
ET

endstream
endobj
